Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0,"per_horizon":false}

Thought: Evaluate the raw inverse‑error weighted combination (w5) to see if it can beat the current median leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w5","rationale":"test raw inverse‑error weights"}

Thought: Reduce model redundancy first; a pruned pool should give cleaner weights or robust aggregates.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: try inverse‑error weights with moderate shrinkage and per‑horizon to reduce variance on the pruned pool.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5,"per_horizon":true}  

Thought: evaluate weighted combination using the new shrinkage‑per‑horizon weights.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w6","rationale":"inverse‑error weights with shrinkage 0.5 and per‑horizon"}  

Thought: try error‑trend weighting to adapt to the strong downward trend across windows.  
Action: weights_error_trend  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"mae","eta":1.0,"damping":null}  

Thought: evaluate weighted combination using the error‑trend weights on the pruned pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w7","rationale":"error‑trend weights on pruned pool"}

